x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 variant of an *inline* constructor on this target and cxx1 emits C1 and C2 - the difference base-implicit-constructor-emitted.nonames records; a class template's constructor cannot be moved out of line to dodge it. The member-template names themselves agree on every target since 2026-10-02, when the Itanium name began to be spelled from the pattern signature (S_IXT_EE for V<M>::head's return) rather than the substituted one.
